&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grandstand (Nasdaq: GRSD) is the intelligence layer of sports, gaming and entertainment.&lt;/strong&gt; We build the brands people trust, the data our partners depend on, and the technology this industry runs on with exceptional people, not shortcuts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;OpticOdds delivers enterprise-grade data infrastructure to B2B partners worldwide, while OddsJam and RotoWire put that same real-time intelligence directly into the hands of consumers.&amp;nbsp; On the gaming and entertainment side, our portfolio includes some of the biggest names in the space: &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Gambling.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Gambling.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Casinos.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Casinos.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Spotlight.Vegas&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Spotlight.Vegas&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://WhichBingo.co.uk&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;WhichBingo.co.uk&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; Our flagship sites reach millions of consumers every month.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re the first, and only, U.S. publicly traded company of our kind, and the first company to win EGR&#39;s Affiliate of the Year three times. We hold every hire to the same five standards: Taste, Agency, Speed, Craft, Responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior CRM Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;, you will play a pivotal role in driving the commercial success of our CRM programme. You&#39;ll take ownership of customer journey optimisation, testing, segmentation and automation across multiple brands and international markets, ensuring every communication is designed to maximise engagement, retention and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with Commercial, Product, Data and Operations teams, you&#39;ll identify opportunities to improve customer lifecycle marketing, build sophisticated automated journeys and continually optimise performance through data-driven decision making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who is commercially minded, highly analytical and naturally curious, someone who enjoys solving problems, learning new technologies quickly and taking ownership of delivering measurable business results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of CRM performance across all customer communications, continually identifying opportunities to increase engagement, conversion, retention and overall revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the CRM testing roadmap, developing a culture of continuous experimentation through A/B and multivariate testing across customer journeys, content, timing, segmentation and personalisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve customer segmentation strategies, ensuring every communication reaches the right customer at the right time using behavioural, transactional and lifecycle data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously analyse journey performance, proactively identifying opportunities to optimise automations, improve customer experience and maximise commercial return.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take responsibility for identifying new CRM opportunities independently, bringing forward ideas backed by data and seeing them through to implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build and optimise automated customer lifecycle journeys across acquisition, onboarding, engagement, retention and reactivation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop dynamic and personalised CRM campaigns across Email, SMS, Push Notifications and emerging engagement channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Commercial, Product, Data and Operations teams to ensure CRM activity supports wider business objectives and revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimise landing pages that support CRM campaigns and improve conversion performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor campaign performance and produce regular reporting with clear commercial insights and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain excellent database hygiene, customer segmentation and GDPR compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI-powered tools to accelerate campaign creation, reporting, analysis and personalisation while maintaining high editorial standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed on emerging CRM technologies, AI capabilities and industry best practices, recommending new approaches that improve team performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and mentor junior CRM team members while promoting best practices across the wider business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years&#39; experience in CRM, Lifecycle Marketing or Marketing Automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience delivering measurable commercial growth through CRM optimisation and customer lifecycle marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building and managing complex automated customer journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of customer segmentation, personalisation and lifecycle marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading structured testing programmes and using data to drive commercial decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical with the ability to identify opportunities independently and take ownership through to delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, self-starting mindset with excellent problem-solving skills and a willingness to learn quickly in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident working autonomously, researching solutions and driving projects forward with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple brands and priorities simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience within the online gambling, sports betting or affiliate marketing industry, with a proven track record of delivering successful CRM initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using &lt;strong&gt;Bloomreach Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with HTML/CSS for email development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using reporting platforms such as Tableau, Power BI or Looker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI-assisted tools to improve CRM production, reporting and customer personalisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who doesn&#39;t wait to be told what to do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be naturally curious, commercially minded and constantly looking for ways to improve performance. You&#39;ll enjoy digging into data, finding opportunities others have missed and taking ownership of delivering measurable results. You&#39;re someone who learns quickly, thrives on solving problems independently and is comfortable challenging the status quo in pursuit of better customer experiences and stronger commercial outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be equally comfortable collaborating with stakeholders across the business or rolling up your sleeves to build, test and optimise campaigns yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perks &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive private Healthcare Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work environment and home office available&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gym &amp;amp; Leisure Allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All the hardware and software you need to be successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company events and social outings, activities, Spot Awards and a Monthly Social Club&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to courses for Personal and Career Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Paid Volunteer Day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Qube Research &amp;amp; Technologies (QRT) is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating in all liquid asset classes across the world. We are a technology and data driven group implementing a scientific approach to investing. Combining data, research, technology and trading expertise has shaped QRT’s collaborative mindset which enables us to solve the most complex challenges. QRT’s culture of innovation continuously drives our ambition to deliver high quality returns for our investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;We are looking for an experienced AI Engineer to help drive the adoption of AI across our High Frequency Trading (HFT) business. You will build AI-powered tools, agents, and platforms that improve productivity across research, development, and trading operations.&amp;nbsp;You will evaluate emerging AI technologies, integrate them into our internal ecosystem, and develop solutions that deliver measurable business value.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your future role within QRT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Build and maintain AI-powered applications, assistants, and agentic workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop integrations between AI systems and internal tools, repositories, databases, and knowledge sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement AI agents capable of interacting with enterprise systems and APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new models, frameworks, and AI tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Partner with researchers, engineers, and business teams to identify high-value use cases&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to standards and best practices for AI development across the HFT business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your present skillset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Strong software engineering experience in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent design, debugging, and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern AI platforms, LLMs, and AI tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of APIs, distributed systems, and software architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently drive projects from conception to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI agents or agentic workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating AI systems and coding assistants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with MCPs, tool-use frameworks, or related technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with quantitative research, trading technology, or financial markets (good-to-have)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;main-content&quot; class=&quot;wiki-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;QRT is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome diversity as essential to our success. QRT empowers employees to work openly and respectfully to achieve collective success. In addition to professional achievement, we are offering initiatives and programs to enable employees achieve a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;likes-and-labels-container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;likes-section&quot; class=&quot;no-print&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Qube Research &amp;amp; Technologies (QRT) is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating in all liquid asset classes across the world. We are a technology and data driven group implementing a scientific approach to investing. Combining data, research, technology, and trading expertise has shaped QRT’s collaborative mindset which enables us to solve the most complex challenges. QRT’s culture of innovation continuously drives our ambition to deliver high quality returns for our investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an exceptional Data Scientist. In this role, you will work between the Research and Trading desks, and the Engineering team to ensure the successful leveraging of data at the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your future role within QRT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team is integral to the firm’s success. As such, your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with Quantitative Researchers and Traders to design datasets that drive systematic strategies and to inform discretionary trading decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototyping and designing code to extract, clean, and aggregate data from a wide range of raw sources and formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with Engineers to automate and optimise your code, ensuring robust data extraction processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the end-to-end process of onboarding new datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively solving data related problems to minimise time to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovating and experimenting with novel data extraction methods to enhance the firm’s data onboarding toolkit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your present skillset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as a Data Scientist (or similar position); experience in a buy-side quantitative finance role is advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Postgraduate degree in a quantitative discipline such as Mathematics, Physics or Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced programming experience in Python, including proficiency with data handling libraries such as Pandas and NumPy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable interest in financial markets and the application of data in its analysis and understanding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with both traditional and alternative financial datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to effectively collaborate with all stakeholders, including researchers, traders, engineers, management, and external vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a high-performance, high-velocity environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;QRT is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome diversity as essential to our success. QRT empowers employees to work openly and respectfully to achieve collective success. In addition to professional achievement, we are offering initiatives and programs to enable employees achieve a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;135&quot; data-end=&quot;148&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;218&quot;&gt;Own the firmware that brings Graphcore hardware and silicon to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;220&quot; data-end=&quot;431&quot;&gt;As a Staff Firmware Engineer, you will design, develop and deliver firmware for Graphcore’s next generation products. Your work will sit close to the hardware and shape how our systems boot, run and communicate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;433&quot; data-end=&quot;633&quot;&gt;You will help build the software that supports complete hardware bootup, silicon interaction, telemetry and monitoring. Your code will connect silicon, drivers, host systems and datacentre operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;635&quot; data-end=&quot;831&quot;&gt;You will take part in technical design discussions across Graphcore and with partners. You will also help engineers solve complex firmware problems and raise engineering standards across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;833&quot; data-end=&quot;961&quot;&gt;This role suits someone who wants deep technical ownership, real system complexity and the chance to influence product delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;963&quot; data-end=&quot;983&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;985&quot; data-end=&quot;1164&quot;&gt;The Firmware team writes the software that enables Graphcore hardware and silicon to start, operate and report reliably. The work is practical, technical and close to the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1166&quot; data-end=&quot;1341&quot;&gt;Engineers are expected to own outcomes, speak up in design discussions and move work forward. Decisions are shaped through technical debate, code reviews and Agile ceremonies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1343&quot; data-end=&quot;1529&quot;&gt;You will work with firmware specialists, system software engineers, partners and wider product teams. The pace is focused, with responsibility shared by people who understand the detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1531&quot; data-end=&quot;1553&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1555&quot; data-end=&quot;2056&quot;&gt;· Strong embedded software engineering experience using C or C++&lt;br&gt;· Experience designing and implementing real-time embedded systems using Zephyr or a similar RTOS&lt;br&gt;· Proven ability to understand, build and debug complex embedded platforms&lt;br&gt;· Clear problem-solving skills and the ability to drive outcomes independently&lt;br&gt;· Strong communication skills, including documenting complex system designs clearly&lt;br&gt;· Solid understanding of Continuous Integration, build systems and software packaging best practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2058&quot; data-end=&quot;2270&quot;&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2272&quot; data-end=&quot;2280&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2282&quot; data-end=&quot;3180&quot;&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work Comment by Helen Doyle: can we take out unlimited as its not contractual and change to generous or flexible.&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3182&quot; data-end=&quot;3544&quot;&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3546&quot; data-end=&quot;3557&quot;&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3559&quot; data-end=&quot;3715&quot;&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3717&quot; data-end=&quot;3743&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3745&quot; data-end=&quot;4024&quot;&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4026&quot; data-end=&quot;4308&quot;&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4310&quot; data-end=&quot;4632&quot;&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4634&quot; data-end=&quot;4776&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;If you want to shape the firmware behind Graphcore’s next generation systems, we’d love to hear from you. Apply now to be part of the journey.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;DRW are looking for a Software Engineer to join the Commodities trading group to build data pipelines for the ingestion and analysis of datasets. The role entails working closely with senior data engineers and key stakeholders across both green field and established projects. Initially it will be focused on getting data to our analysts, with &amp;nbsp;opportunities to help design and build the core data infrastructure used across the group as your experience grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How you will make an impact…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development of reliable ETL pipelines in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on a small team alongside experienced engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular direct contact with internal users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a mixture of both legacy and greenfield projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you bring to the team…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s or master’s in a numeric degree or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python programming experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiastic, motivated, and detail-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DRW is a diversified trading firm with over 3 decades of experience bringing sophisticated technology and exceptional people together to operate in markets around the world. &amp;nbsp;We value autonomy and the ability to quickly pivot to capture opportunities, so we operate using our own capital and trading at our own risk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Chicago with offices throughout the U.S., Canada, Europe, and Asia, we trade a variety of asset classes including Fixed Income, ETFs, Equities, FX, Commodities and Energy across all major global markets. We have also leveraged our expertise and technology to expand into three non-traditional strategies: real estate, venture capital and cryptoassets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate with respect, curiosity and open minds. The people who thrive here share our belief that it’s not just what we do that matters–it&#39;s how we do it. &amp;nbsp;DRW is a place of high expectations, integrity, innovation and a willingness to challenge consensus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the following statement at the bottom of all job postings:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For more information about DRW&#39;s processing activities and our use of job applicants&#39; data, please view our Privacy Notice at &lt;a href=&quot;https://drw.com/privacy-notice&quot;&gt;https://drw.com/privacy-notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California residents, please review the&amp;nbsp;California Privacy Notice&amp;nbsp;for information about certain legal rights at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://drw.com/california-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;https://drw.com/california-privacy-notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Lodestar&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lodestar&#39;s mission is to develop the first &quot;Protect and Defend&quot; capability for high-value space assets in orbit. Our flagship product, MITHRIL, is our hardware-agnostic, AI-enabled autonomy software suite that enables us to augment any off-the-shelf spacecraft with the ability to autonomously detect, characterise, and reversibly neutralise orbital threats. By building on the proven space heritage of our best-in-class satellite-bus partners and fully integrating MITHRIL into a single unified platform, we deliver an end-to-end, autonomous in-space bodyguarding service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring &lt;strong&gt;Avionics Software Engineers&lt;/strong&gt; across three technical focus areas: &lt;strong&gt;Flight Software, Distributed Middleware &amp;amp; Embedded Linux&lt;/strong&gt; Depending on your experience, you’ll take ownership of one of these areas while working closely across avionics, autonomy, AI/ML, and hardware.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within our Avionics Software team, we&#39;re hiring multiple engineers across three core technical specialisms. Please identify which role best matches your skills and experience:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Flight Software Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop deterministic, safety-critical, fault tolerant flight software for autonomous spacecraft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build robust software for RTOS-based flight computers, implementing FDIR and defensive programming techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with autonomy, AI, and hardware engineers to integrate, test, and validate mission-critical software on representative spacecraft platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Distributed Middleware Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the distributed middleware enabling communication, workload orchestration, and telemetry across heterogeneous onboard compute systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build resilient software infrastructure including high-performance IPC, networking, process supervision, and fail-safe Over-The-Air (OTA) update mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver scalable software platforms that support fault-tolerant autonomous operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Embedded Linux Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain custom embedded Linux platforms for NVIDIA Jetson-based flight computers, from board bring-up through to deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimise kernel performance through real-time tuning, low-level driver development, system profiling and selective kernel slimming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect a hardened, minimal-footprint Linux-based operating system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following qualifications are desired across all three roles:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BEng/MEng in Engineering, Computer Science, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing software for embedded systems using Linux or RTOS (e.g., RTEMS, FreeRTOS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of multi-process architectures and inter-process communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator and self-starter; able to work independently and in a collaborative team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated skills in debugging and performance characterisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Desired skills and experience relevant to the three roles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of communication protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerisation and deployment tools (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of Linux kernel architecture, bootloaders (e.g., U-Boot), and low-level system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of fault-tolerant design principles, error handling, or defensive programming in resource-constrained systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time Linux kernel tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background with the space industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with publish-subscribe middlewares.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to fail-safe Over-The-Air (OTA) update frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated strong problem-solving skills and ability to work in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in system integration and working with multidisciplinary teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pay Range:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(E1) Junior Engineer: £30,000 - £55,000 / year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(E2) Mid-level Engineer: £55,000 - £75,000 / year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful equity incentives as part of our employee option pool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 Days Annual Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental &amp;amp; vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributory pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be part of a scrappy, dynamic, multidisciplinary, collaborative crew 🏴‍☠️&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Information:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For security reasons background checks will be undertaken prior to any employment offers being made to an applicant. These checks will include nationality checks as it is a requirement of this position that you be eligible to access equipment and data regulated by the United States&#39; International Traffic in Arms Regulations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Under these Regulations, you may be ineligible for this role if you do not hold citizenship of one of the following countries: Albania, Australia, Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Canada, Croatia, Cyprus, Czech Republic, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Iceland, Ireland, Italy, Japan, Latvia, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta, Montenegro, Netherlands, New Zealand, North Macedonia, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovakia, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden, Switzerland, Turkey, United Kingdom, or United States, or if you hold ineligible dual citizenship or nationality. For more information on these Regulations, click here &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2020/01/23/2020-00574/international-traffic-in-arms-regulations-us-munitions-list-categories-i-ii-and-iii&quot;&gt;ITAR Regulations.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Additional Information:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation bands are determined by role, level, location, and alignment with market data. Individual level and base pay is determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on job-related skills, education, experience, technical capabilities and internal equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lodestar is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

